## Decision Record

- Codex remains the human interaction layer; deterministic scripts remain the guarded mutation and
  projection layer.
- Reuse executive-directive Ideas, planning order, relationships, outcomes, and reconciliation.
- Store human directive progress in the directive contract rather than inferring it from unrelated
  artifact counts.
- Render evidence-backed milestone checkboxes and explain partial local completion plus external
  gates truthfully.
- Preserve a concise main cockpit and retain exhaustive accounting as drill-down.
- Preserve operator choice: recommend one next action but never start it from the read-only view.

## Recovery Contract

- Existing generated marker, atomic refresh, exact-byte freshness check, SQLite/file authority, and
  checkpoint/rebuild behavior remain intact.
- Missing or malformed human status data degrades to an explicit needs-attention card; it never
  fabricates completion or silently drops a directive.
- Existing directives without the extended capsule remain readable through a compatibility
  projection and can be enriched conversationally.
- Failed development deployment does not alter production or close the owning outcome.

## Verification Strategy

- Focused tests for directive parsing, lifecycle commands, ordering, checkbox evidence, status
  rollup, recommendation selection, compatibility fallback, deterministic rendering, and hosted
  payload/template parity.
- DisplayTest-shaped fixtures proving that completed foundations are checked, physical gates remain
  unchecked, and the recommended next action is visible without interpreting internal IDs.
- Existing project-projection, directive, dashboard, documentation, manifest, and full repository
  validation.
- Work2 deployment and changed-behavior checks on the configured Linux and Windows disposable test
  beds, followed by release-cohort registration without production promotion.

## Authority Boundaries

This roadmap authorizes faithful planning, local source/test/documentation changes, managed
artifacts and outcomes, a scoped local commit, deployment to the configured disposable Linux and
Windows development targets, changed-behavior verification, and Work2 release-cohort registration.
It does not authorize production release, push, publication, live DisplayTest mutation, credentials,
destructive recovery, or continuous synchronization of arbitrary strategy files.

